2026-11-07T06:37:21.4219500Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4254940Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4256620Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4257870Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4258370Z 
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4258750Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4259430Z 
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4259850Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4260810Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4261320Z 
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4261730Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4262380Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4262840Z 
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4263270Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:37:21.4264070Z   $ sh ./install-nix
